 linen napkin, introducing a touch of quiet elegance.  \n\nNatural light streams through a large window at the far end, framed by a thin white trim, illuminating the space with soft daylight. The floor beneath the table is covered with a woven area rug in geometric patterns composed of deep red, olive green, charcoal, and mustard yellow, anchoring the seating area and echoing the color story of the room.  \n\nAccent lighting includes a sleek black metal wall sconce mounted near the dining zone, angled downward to cast focused illumination. On the opposite wall, a framed artwork depicting stylized animals in bold red, ochre, and black adds a graphic focal point, enhancing the room’s artistic character. The overall atmosphere is one of calm sophistication, where neutral foundations are elevated by intentional bursts of color and texture—especially in the terracotta upholstery, the multi-hued rug, and the vibrant artwork—creating a harmonious yet dynamic interior experience.","Using the materials, color schemes, and style shown in Figure 2, transform the white-matte image in Figure 1 into a high-end, photorealistic interior rendering. Strictly adhere to the style, color palette, and materials of Figure 2 when transferring all elements from Figure 1, ensuring that the final result achieves photo-realistic fidelity. Maintain the spatial structure and layout of Figure 1 exactly as they are; do not add any new objects. The floor, walls, ceiling, and accent colors in Figure 1 should be generated using the same materials as those specified in Figure 2., A minimalist kitchen and dining space rendered in a warm, mid-century modern aesthetic, featuring a rich palette of earthy tones and carefully curated accent colors. The walls are finished in a soft beige tone with subtle texture, complementing the light wood flooring that extends throughout the room, laid in a herringbone pattern for added depth. The ceiling is painted in a warm off-white, hosting a single round flush-mount 